Here's an implementation of ternary search in Python:

```
def ternary_search(arr, left, right, x):

    if right >= left:

        mid1 = left + (right - left) // 3
        mid2 = right - (right - left) // 3

        if arr[mid1] == x:
            return mid1
        elif arr[mid2] == x:
            return mid2
        elif x < arr[mid1]:
            return ternary_search(arr, left, mid1-1, x)
        elif x > arr[mid2]:
            return ternary_search(arr, mid2+1, right, x)
        else:
            return ternary_search(arr, mid1+1, mid2-1, x)

    return -1
```

To use this function, pass in the array `arr`, the left and right indices of the subarray you want to search, and the target value `x`. Call the function like this:

```
